  "description": "The kara-mon or kara-kado (唐門) is a type of gate seen in Japanese architecture.  It is characterized by the usage of kara-hafu, an undulating bargeboard peculiar to Japan.  Kara-mon are often used at the entrances of Japanese castles, Buddhist temples and Shinto shrines, and have historically been a symbol of authority.",
